I have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

## Summary of findings

This is a Spring PetClinic variant with a parallel "OfficeFloor" functional pipeline for `POST /api/owners`. The owner-create business logic lives in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`, wired together by the YAML flow in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. A key observation up front: the acceptance test asserts a *target/future* behavior (deterministic `householdId` from `lastName`+`postcode`) that the current code does NOT yet implement — the current code derives `householdId` from `lastName`+`address` and only assigns it when `sharesHousehold=true`.

---

### 1. Where householdId is currently generated/assigned (pre-deterministic logic)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java`
The current logic only assigns a `householdId` when the request opts in with `sharesHousehold=true` AND an existing owner already occupies the same household (same last name + normalized address). It reuses an existing member's id if present, otherwise derives one via `Household.idFor(...)` and back-fills it onto existing members:

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    List<Owner> members = new ArrayList<>();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findByLastName(request.getLastName())) {
        if (Household.matches(existing, request.getLastName(), request.getAddress())) {
            members.add(existing);
        }
    }
    if (members.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }
    String householdId = members.stream()
            .map(Owner::getHouseholdId)
            .filter(id -> id != null && !id.isBlank())
            .findFirst()
            .orElseGet(() -> Household.idFor(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress()));
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner member : members) {
        if (!householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId())) {
            member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(member);
        }
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Household.java`
Defines household identity and the id derivation. Currently keyed on `lastName` (canonicalized) + normalized **address** — NOT postcode:

```java
static String canonical(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.strip().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}

static boolean matches(Owner owner, String lastName, String address) {
    return canonical(owner.getLastName()).equals(canonical(lastName))
            && AddressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress()).equals(AddressNormalizer.normalize(address));
}

static String idFor(String lastName, String address) {
    String hex = Sha256.hex(canonical(lastName) + '|' + AddressNormalizer.normalize(address));
    return "H-" + hex.substring(0, 12);
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Sha256.java` — the hashing helper used for the household id (returns full UPPER-case hex).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — the entity field/getter/setter:
```java
@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;
```
(lines 69-70, getter/setter lines 159-165)

Flow ordering (`owners.POST.yml`): `build -> assignHousehold -> ensureUniqueIdentity -> countHouseholdMembers -> ... -> countNamesakes -> assignMembershipLevel -> detectPossibleDuplicate -> save`. All under `govern: [ transaction ]`.

---

### 2. Where "sharesHousehold" is read/used

Only one reader in Java:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java` line 21: `if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold()))`.

Defined as a request-only field in the OpenAPI schema (this generates `OwnerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold()` — the DTO is code-generated from the spec; no hand-written DTO source exists):
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2067-2074:
```yaml
sharesHousehold:
  title: Shares household
  description: >-
    Request-only opt-in acknowledging that this owner deliberately shares a household with an
    existing owner. When true, the create endpoint skips the duplicate-household rejection that
    fires when another owner already has the same last name and address.
  type: boolean
  example: true
```
Used in the acceptance test at `AcceptanceTest.java` line 22 (`b.put("sharesHousehold", true)`).

---

### 3. Where duplicate detection happens (409 / conflict)

Hard duplicate (returns 409):
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` — the single duplicate check. Compares the derived identity key against existing owners sharing the telephone; throws `DuplicateIdentityException`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findByTelephone(owner.getTelephone())) {
        if (identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException(identityKey);
        }
    }
}
```

The identity key itself is derived on the entity:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 258-265:
```java
@Transient
public String getIdentityKey() {
    return blankToEmpty(this.telephone) + '|' + blankToEmpty(this.email) + '|' + blankToEmpty(this.householdId);
}
```

Exception + handler (the 409 response):
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java`:
```java
public void handle(@Parameter DuplicateIdentityException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Map<String, List<String>>>> response) {
    response.send(new ResponseEntity<>(Map.of("errors", List.of("identityKey")), HttpStatus.CONFLICT));
}
```
Wired by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`.

Soft duplicate (still created, sets a flag — does NOT 409):
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DetectPossibleDuplicate.java` — flags a match on last name + postcode but different telephone via `setPossibleDuplicateOf`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
        return;
    }
    ownerRepository.findByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .filter(existing -> existing.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName())
            && postcode.equals(existing.getPostcode())
            && existing.getTelephone() != null
            && !existing.getTelephone().equals(owner.getTelephone()))
        .map(Owner::getId)
        .filter(id -> id != null)
        .min(Integer::compareTo)
        .ifPresent(owner::setPossibleDuplicateOf);
}
```
Backing fields/getters `possibleDuplicateOf` / transient `getPossibleDuplicate()` in `Owner.java` lines 81-82, 196-211.

---

### 4. Where household-size is computed and fed into membership level

Household size computation:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CountHouseholdMembers.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
    if (householdId == null || householdId.isBlank()) {
        owner.setHouseholdSize(1);
        return;
    }
    long existing = ownerRepository.findByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .filter(member -> householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId()))
        .count();
    owner.setHouseholdSize((int) (existing + 1));
}
```

Membership level calculation:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java`:
```java
private static final int MAX_LEVEL_ON_CREATION = 3;

public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    int level = 1;
    if (StringUtils.hasText(owner.getEmail())) {
        level++;
    }
    if (Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount())) {
        level++;
    }
    owner.setMembershipLevel(Math.min(level, MAX_LEVEL_ON_CREATION));
}
```

IMPORTANT gap: `householdSize` is computed and stored, but `AssignMembershipLevel` currently does NOT read it — the level today depends only on `email` presence and `namesakeCount`. My grep confirms the only readers of `getHouseholdSize()` are the setter callers in `CountHouseholdMembers`; nothing feeds household size into the level yet. The namesake count that IS used is set by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CountNamesakes.java`.

Also note `householdSize` is persisted (`Owner.householdSize`, column `household_size`) but is NOT exposed in the OpenAPI `Owner` schema (no `householdSize` property there — only `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `membershipLevel`).

---

### 5. Relevant DTOs, requests, entities, repositories, OfficeFloor functions, escalation handlers

Entity / model:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — fields `householdId`, `householdSize`, `membershipLevel`, `namesakeCount`, `possibleDuplicateOf`; transient `getIdentityKey()`, `getPossibleDuplicate()`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` — `lastName`/`firstName` fields (lines 40, 50-55) and `initials()`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Sha256.java` — hash helper for household id.

DTO / request (generated from spec — no hand-written source files exist):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — schema `OwnerFields` (input incl. `sharesHousehold`, `lastName`, `postcode`) lines 1991-2080; schema `Owner` (output incl. `householdId` 2145, `namesakeCount` 2153, `membershipLevel` 2163, `identityKey` 2201, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` 2210-2228). These generate `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct mapper Owner<->DTO; `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` used by `BuildOwner`, `toOwnerDto(...)` used by the response function.

Repository:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` — `findByLastName(String)` line 47, `findByLastName(String, Pageable)` line 49, `findByTelephone(String)` line 68. These are the queries backing all the household/duplicate lookups. (Impls under `repository/jpa`, `repository/jdbc`, `repository/springdatajpa`.)

OfficeFloor function classes (`rest/function/owner/`) touching these concepts:
- `AssignHousehold.java`, `Household.java` (package-private helper), `CountHouseholdMembers.java`, `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`, `DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`, `AssignMembershipLevel.java`, `CountNamesakes.java`, `BuildOwner.java`, `ApplyOwner.java`, `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java`, `AddressNormalizer.java`, `ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`, `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`.

OfficeFloor resource files:
- Flow: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (full step chain quoted above).
- Escalation wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml` (and the sibling escalation ymls for the other handlers in that directory).

Escalation handlers/exceptions (in `rest/escalation/`):
- `DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` (the 409 for hard duplicates).
- Related handlers exist for the other rules (`InvalidPostcodeException(Handler)`, `CityAtCapacityException(Handler)`, etc.) but only the DuplicateIdentity pair is relevant to duplicate detection.

---

### 6. Existing tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the single household test, `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId()`. Its header comment states the TARGET contract: "householdId is deterministic from (lastName, postcode) alone." It asserts:
- two owners with same lastName + postcode "2000" (second with `sharesHousehold=true`) get the SAME `householdId`;
- a third owner with a different lastName, same postcode, and NO `sharesHousehold` still returns a `householdId` that differs.

Note: this test expects behavior the current `AssignHousehold`/`Household` code does not produce (current logic keys on address not postcode, and only assigns an id when `sharesHousehold=true` with existing members — so owner `c` would currently have a null `householdId`). This is the spec the deterministic refactor must satisfy.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the black-box harness (helpers `ownerNode()`, `uniqueLastName()`, `withPostcode()`, `createOwnerOk()`, `fetchOwner()`, `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn`, pinned region/postcode tables). Tests hit only `POST /api/owners` and read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

No other test files reference household, membership level, duplicate detection, or identity key.

---

